# Cloudflare *appends* every matching rule rather than letting the most
# specific one win, so `/*` must not set Cache-Control — see the landing's
# copy of this file. The SPA shell keeps the platform default
# (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate), which is exactly right: a cached shell
# that outlived its asset hashes is a blank page.
#
# X-Robots-Tag is the header twin of the noindex in index.html: the app is
# per-user and wallet-gated, so nothing on this origin belongs in search. The
# header also covers what the meta tag can't (assets, robots.txt, and any
# crawler that reads headers before HTML). robots.txt leaves crawling open so
# both signals are actually seen.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Vite fingerprints these.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
